# Materialized as `.gitignore`.
#
# ONLY `kata-out/`, and only because the gold workflow's validate stage writes
# its evidence log there. The suite itself is `sh tests/test_tail.sh` and writes
# NOTHING — no build directory, no lockfile, no interpreter home — which is the
# other half of why a shell subject was chosen over a compiled or interpreted
# one.
#
# This entry is load-bearing twice:
#   * the declared write closure (`produces_files = ["kata-out/check.log"]`)
#     is judged at delta adoption, so every write the check makes must land
#     inside it; `kata-out/` holds them all.
#   * `require_promotable_workspace_for_promotion` computes dirtiness from
#     `git status --porcelain` WITHOUT `--ignored`, so an un-ignored evidence log
#     would refuse the promote AFTER a human had already approved it.
/kata-out/

# ── REQUIRED BY KATA, and its absence silently corrupts the trunk ──────
#
# kata materializes each execution's candidate workspace at
# `<vcs.jj_repo>/agents/<execution-id>/` and keeps jj's own state in `.jj/`.
# BOTH are INSIDE the repository kata is pointed at, so a repo that does not
# ignore them sees them as ordinary untracked files.
#
# The failure is silent rather than loud: with these two entries missing, the
# gold loop runs green end to end — validate passes, the human gate parks, the
# approval goes through — and the promote then lands jj's internal index and the
# whole candidate worktree, while `src/tally.sh` at the repo root is NEVER
# CHANGED. The agent's actual fix does not land, and every surface reports
# success.
#
# kata's own repository carries exactly these two entries, with a comment naming
# this case — so this is a REQUIREMENT kata places on any repo it is pointed at,
# and today nothing checks it. Registered as a `kata doctor` gap.
.jj/
/agents/
